      "sequence_position": 19,
      "problem": "Let\n$p=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ y-3 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $q=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].$\nIf $p\\cdot q=0$, find the value of $y.$",
      "worked_solution": "Starting from the equation $p\\cdot q=0,$ we compute the dot product in terms of $y$ and then solve for $y$ in the resulting equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 9\\cdot 0+(y-3)\\cdot 1+3\\cdot (-4)+4\\cdot y & =0 \\\\ y-3-12+4y & =0 \\\\ 5y & =15 \\\\ y & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y=3.$",
